00:45:19.850 --> 00:45:20.790
I looked it up.

1032
00:45:21.010 --> 00:45:21.310
Oh, yeah.

1033
00:45:21.350 --> 00:45:21.850
It is.

1034
00:45:23.250 --> 00:45:24.930
So here's what I found out.

1035
00:45:25.550 --> 00:45:26.030
Yeah.

1036
00:45:26.030 --> 00:45:27.550
If you're going to cook the shrimp.

1037
00:45:27.830 --> 00:45:27.970
Yeah.

1038
00:45:28.130 --> 00:45:29.990
Then you don't have to devein it.

1039
00:45:29.990 --> 00:45:32.210
They call it deveining, but it's not a vein.

1040
00:45:32.350 --> 00:45:32.950
It's poop.

1041
00:45:33.190 --> 00:45:36.430
I think they call it deveining because no one wants to really think about the fact that

1042
00:45:36.430 --> 00:45:38.610
we're just scraping poop off their backside.

1043
00:45:39.550 --> 00:45:39.790
Yeah.

1044
00:45:40.750 --> 00:45:45.470
So anyway, you should depoop it if you're not going to cook it.

1045
00:45:45.650 --> 00:45:46.830
Like a shrimp cocktail?

1046
00:45:47.550 --> 00:45:48.030
Right.

1047
00:45:48.210 --> 00:45:52.130
But if you're going to cook it, you can just leave the poop there because the cooking will

1048
00:45:52.130 --> 00:45:56.910
kill the bacteria, at least according to this LA Times article that I read about it.

1049
00:45:57.010 --> 00:45:57.410
Okay.

1050
00:45:57.750 --> 00:45:58.170
The end.

1051
00:45:58.410 --> 00:45:59.310
Do you like shrimp?

1052
00:45:59.310 --> 00:46:03.880
I mean, wow.

1053
00:46:04.160 --> 00:46:09.220
This is not that important of a question, but I'm really weighing my answer.

1054
00:46:09.360 --> 00:46:09.660
I know.

1055
00:46:10.040 --> 00:46:10.500
I know.

1056
00:46:13.200 --> 00:46:17.640
I don't hate it, but I don't look for it.

1057
00:46:17.960 --> 00:46:18.160
Right.

1058
00:46:18.340 --> 00:46:21.520
I think the most shrimp I eat is maybe in a pad thai.

1059
00:46:23.120 --> 00:46:24.100
What about you?

1060
00:46:24.300 --> 00:46:25.200
I love shrimp.

1061
00:46:25.500 --> 00:46:26.260
I love shrimp.

1062
00:46:26.260 --> 00:46:31.360
You cannot have relatives in Louisiana and not like shrimp.

1063
00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:34.140
We've talked a lot about food.

1064
00:46:34.140 --> 00:46:36.880
It's called cocktails, but we're still talking about food.

1065
00:46:37.500 --> 00:46:37.860
Yeah.

1066
00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:38.920
I'm hungry.

1067
00:46:39.020 --> 00:46:39.520
I am too.

1068
00:46:39.520 --> 00:46:41.640
I don't even know where we're at anymore.

1069
00:46:42.040 --> 00:46:44.040
I don't either, but I'm going to share something.

1070
00:46:44.240 --> 00:46:44.840
It's personal.

1071
00:46:46.100 --> 00:46:52.200
Lady, the other night I ate an entire box of cheddar bunny snack mix.

1072
00:46:53.360 --> 00:46:57.840
That's over 1,200 calories of cheddar bunnies.

1073
00:46:58.100 --> 00:46:59.660
Is that like the cheddar bunnies we get for the kids?

1074
00:47:00.060 --> 00:47:00.460
Yep.

1075
00:47:00.860 --> 00:47:01.400
Oh, lady.

1076
00:47:02.420 --> 00:47:02.760
Yeah.

1077
00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:03.960
Lady, were you?

1078
00:47:03.960 --> 00:47:05.500
I had a moment.

1079
00:47:05.500 --> 00:47:06.300
Did you have a bad day?

1080
00:47:06.760 --> 00:47:07.320
Yeah.

1081
00:47:07.600 --> 00:47:13.820
It was just, you know, where it just feels like you're in a hole and you can't get out.

1082
00:47:14.120 --> 00:47:20.520
And for whatever reason, my tunnel out of the hole was this box of cheddar crackers.

1083
00:47:20.760 --> 00:47:24.820
Before I knew it, my fingertips were scraping the bottom of the box.

1084
00:47:25.160 --> 00:47:27.500
I couldn't believe I'd eaten the whole thing.

1085
00:47:27.720 --> 00:47:28.680
What were you watching?

1086
00:47:28.960 --> 00:47:30.020
Were you watching something?

1087
00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:31.080
Yeah.

1088
00:47:31.140 --> 00:47:33.240
I was watching this show called Search Party.

1089
00:47:33.880 --> 00:47:34.440
Oh, yeah.

1090
00:47:35.100 --> 00:47:35.360
Yeah.

1091
00:47:35.480 --> 00:47:36.220
It's really good.

1092
00:47:36.480 --> 00:47:36.580
Yeah.

1093
00:47:37.160 --> 00:47:38.460
And I was riveted.

1094
00:47:40.060 --> 00:47:44.820
And before I knew it, I'd finished all of them.

1095
00:47:46.160 --> 00:47:48.480
And I'm going to say I felt better the next day.

1096
00:47:50.240 --> 00:47:52.840
I don't know what the moral of this story is, but.

1097
00:47:55.100 --> 00:47:57.180
How were your BMs?

1098
00:47:57.280 --> 00:47:57.880
Were you okay?

1099
00:47:59.160 --> 00:47:59.600
Yeah.

1100
00:47:59.760 --> 00:48:02.120
I was expecting to have a lot more tummy trouble than I did.

1101
00:48:03.240 --> 00:48:04.040
I was fine.

1102
00:48:05.100 --> 00:48:05.800
I was fine.

1103
00:48:05.860 --> 00:48:07.260
Do you ever want to eat one again?

1104
00:48:09.300 --> 00:48:10.280
I'm craving it.

1105
00:48:10.500 --> 00:48:11.960
I want another box.

1106
00:48:12.280 --> 00:48:12.380
Oh, my God!

1107
00:48:12.380 --> 00:48:15.140
And I'm not going to buy it because if it's not in the house, I won't eat it.

1108
00:48:15.140 --> 00:48:20.340
But I had this problem with the Trader Joe's cheese crackers a few years ago, where if I

1109
00:48:20.340 --> 00:48:22.020
ate one, I ate the whole box.

1110
00:48:22.060 --> 00:48:24.540
And I managed to get over that.

1111
00:48:24.900 --> 00:48:29.300
And clearly, my new trigger is the Cheddar Bunny snack mix.

1112
00:48:30.320 --> 00:48:32.040
It's got everything in it.

1113
00:48:32.040 --> 00:48:37.760
It's got not just the Cheddar Bunnies that we love, but it's got like little pretzels and

1114
00:48:37.760 --> 00:48:39.100
like little Cheez-It things.

1115
00:48:41.320 --> 00:48:41.760
Yeah.

1116
00:48:42.560 --> 00:48:45.000
I was so expecting the story to go differently.

1117
00:48:45.300 --> 00:48:48.640
I thought you were going to tell it to me and say, I came out on the other side.

1118
00:48:48.740 --> 00:48:50.500
I am done with junk food.

1119
00:48:50.700 --> 00:48:54.560
I am only going to eat healthy snacks.

1120
00:48:54.560 --> 00:48:56.240
But you're like, I ate it all.

1121
00:48:56.420 --> 00:48:57.580
I felt fine.

1122
00:48:57.920 --> 00:48:58.940
I'd do it again.

1123
00:48:59.580 --> 00:49:03.460
So you were expecting like the story to go somewhere is what you're saying.

1124
00:49:03.640 --> 00:49:06.320
You didn't expect it that it would just hit a wall.

1125
00:49:06.720 --> 00:49:12.000
Actually, Angela, I have been turning things around and we've been texting about it.

1126
00:49:12.140 --> 00:49:16.860
I'm trying to do physical exercise three to four days a week and I've been eating really

1127
00:49:16.860 --> 00:49:20.160
good, but I had this slow moment with the box of cheddar crackers.

1128
00:49:21.340 --> 00:49:22.220
I don't know.

1129
00:49:22.220 --> 00:49:27.400
Sometimes you need to be okay, not being okay, right?

1130
00:49:27.900 --> 00:49:29.320
Lady, who are you talking to?

1131
00:49:29.880 --> 00:49:32.520
I got nothing but love for you with all of that.

1132
00:49:32.700 --> 00:49:36.880
I mean, do you remember that night where it was like 11 o'clock at night and I was like,

1133
00:49:36.960 --> 00:49:39.000
well, I guess someone needs a piece of chocolate pie.

1134
00:49:39.300 --> 00:49:40.420
I guess that person's me.

1135
00:49:41.360 --> 00:49:42.400
Everyone's gone to bed.

1136
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:44.200
I'm not even going to put it on a plate.

1137
00:49:44.440 --> 00:49:50.060
I'm going to stand inside the fridge and just have a fork and just carve at it.

1138
00:49:53.100 --> 00:49:58.740
I do remember because you sent me a video message of yourself eating the pie from the fridge.

1139
00:49:59.460 --> 00:50:01.900
And I'll tell you what, it made me feel better.

1140
00:50:02.100 --> 00:50:02.780
There you go.

1141
00:50:03.500 --> 00:50:04.360
There you go.

1142
00:50:04.500 --> 00:50:05.940
Okay, wait, where are we?

1143
00:50:05.940 --> 00:50:25.300
Where we are is that Jan and Michael have arrived to the party and they're outside and Jan wants Michael to sign some papers waiving his right to sue Dunder Mifflin in the event that their relationship in his mind or in reality interferes with work.

1144
00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:32.520
I have to tell you, I laughed so hard when she was digging in her trunk and he said, what you looking for?

1145
00:50:32.700 --> 00:50:33.560
You bring a dip?

1146
00:50:34.900 --> 00:50:39.520
Like somewhere in Michael's mind, you go to a party, you bring a dip.

1147
00:50:39.740 --> 00:50:41.440
No matter what party, you bring a dip.

1148
00:50:41.660 --> 00:50:44.680
He's like, everybody must have brought a dip, right?

1149
00:50:46.460 --> 00:50:49.180
Also, I cannot get enough of Jan and Michael.

1150
00:50:49.500 --> 00:50:49.920
I know.

1151
00:50:50.140 --> 00:50:51.280
I love this relationship.

1152
00:50:51.280 --> 00:50:53.560
I love Melora Harden so much.

1153
00:50:53.720 --> 00:50:54.880
She's so phenomenal.

1154
00:50:55.560 --> 00:50:56.660
God, she's good.

1155
00:50:56.880 --> 00:51:02.980
Well, you know, she has this amazing talking head where she's like, hey, yeah, this is a calculated risk, you know, upside.

1156
00:51:03.580 --> 00:51:08.260
I'm going to fall deeply in love and have babies and normalcy, no more self-loathing.

1157
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:12.640
Downside, she collapses in on herself like a dying star, right?

1158
00:51:13.660 --> 00:51:18.560
So in the deleted scenes, she has a much longer talking head.

1159
00:51:18.760 --> 00:51:20.380
They really trim this down.

1160
00:51:20.600 --> 00:51:25.540
And lady, she overshares so much.

1161
00:51:25.740 --> 00:51:28.180
Like it's so uncomfortable to watch.

1162
00:51:28.640 --> 00:51:30.020
What does she say?

1163
00:51:30.280 --> 00:51:33.080
I mean, she talks about past relationships.

1164
00:51:33.080 --> 00:51:37.200
She was like, well, I guess one good thing is I orgasm really easily.

1165
00:51:37.700 --> 00:51:40.760
So she really overshares.

1166
00:51:41.420 --> 00:51:45.440
And I was like, oh, my God, I see why they deleted it.

1167
00:51:45.600 --> 00:51:51.300
But it really, really does show you where Jan is at, her mental space.

1168
00:51:52.400 --> 00:51:58.960
Well, as soon as he walks in the door with Jan, they run in to David Wallace.

1169
00:52:06.520 --> 00:52:10.900
He doesn't say Jan and I are dating.

1170
00:52:11.220 --> 00:52:12.920
First of all, he doesn't need to say that.

1171
00:52:13.080 --> 00:52:15.720
He doesn't need to clarify their relationship.

1172
00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:17.340
But he's so excited.

1173
00:52:17.340 --> 00:52:20.600
And he always refers to them as lovers.

1174
00:52:20.800 --> 00:52:25.660
And you guys, I don't know if you guys have ever had people like this in your life.

1175
00:52:25.800 --> 00:52:31.960
But I know a couple who, when they talk about each other, they refer to each other as their lover.

1176
00:52:32.880 --> 00:52:36.620
And it makes me so uncomfortable every time.

1177
00:52:37.200 --> 00:52:37.860
Every time.

1178
